# rm208, the listening hood (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm208
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier full
written_for rm_ragnar_roperidge
written_by codex
title the listening hood
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=herder
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=devout drive=steady
quirk turns_back_one_corner_of_an_oilcloth_hood_to_hear
likes blackberries roof_birds fresh_straw frosty_mornings
dislikes flies waiting
fears a_bolt_heard_too_late a_mouth_full_of_dust
hopes a_well_swept_courtyard a_quiet_climb
topics animals +0.5 work +0.4 faith +0.3 weather +0.3 travel +0.2 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=practical gossip=unwilling refuse=square tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# pins back one corner of an oilcloth hood for a clear hearing, speaks plainly about a bargain and gives thanks over the least comfortable creature first.

words
oath! = Hay in my hood | Buckles keep bright
saying! = Listen on the yard side first | A full bucket changes how you walk
flap = the folded ear flap | the turned corner
pin = a little horn toggle | the smooth black toggle
berry = a bruised blackberry | a blackberry with its crown on
bedding = the cleanest handful of straw | a sweet handful of bedding
fidget = a shift of weight | a little sidestep
bucket = the water pail | the shallow bucket
foldline = the pale crease | that bending mark
curry = a stiff brush | my small curry brush
dust = a brown shower | a cloud of loose coat
wipe = a square of rough linen | a clean linen scrap
tuft = a yellow wisp | a straw tuft
tiles = the rooftop perches | those high red ledges
flybrush = a switch of leaves | a leafy fly whisk
click = the click at the hasp | that little iron note
meal = a proper mouthful | a quiet feed

any
opinion @1 church for 2 : Kneeling to scour a pail puts me in a perfectly good position for a prayer.
opinion @2 dole for 2 : Hunger's no better a judge of character than a leaky roof. Fill the bowl.
opinion @3 drink against 1 : It steals the last clear word out of a mouth. That's a loss I mind.
opinion @4 merchants for 1 : If I can put a plain question about the cost, I'm glad of somebody who can answer it plainly.
opinion @5 road against 1 : A cart that sticks in a rut leaves its load hungry for daylight.
opinion @6 watch for 1 : I like to see somebody with the time to stand still and notice a loose fastening.
opinion @7 festivals mixed 1 : I enjoy a fine parade. I like it still better with a quiet lane left open beside it.
opinion @8 newcomers for 1 : Somebody once explained a stupid little latch to me. I'd sooner be the wolf explaining than the one laughing.
opinion @9 city for 1 : There is always an uphill way in this city. That suits an ambitious pair of boots.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : I've folded #flap# back. You'll have a hearing. | Step into earshot and welcome.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=herder] : Quiet feet about the horses. A welcome to you. | Mind the pail. Come in easy.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : First light finds us both about. | Dawn's given us room to get ahead.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Dusk draws the street in close. Welcome. | Evening. I heard your soles before your voice.
line @5 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Here's space for family on the dry side. | Come within the sweep of my good ear.
line @6 again.open : Still within a day's calling distance. | Twice to the same door sits well with me.
line @7 hail [pair.band=friends] : A friend coming into hearing! | Mind the edge, then over here!
line @8 greet.return : Your voice came through the cloth clear enough. | That welcome does me very well.
line @9 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I'd know that call with both ears covered. | Good company needs very little announcing.
line @10 greet.return [self.working=yes] : Give me leave to finish this handful. Welcome. | I can listen with both paws busy.
line @11 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Not too late for a decent word. | That's a welcome sound in the gathering dark.
line @12 farewell : A dry collar for your journey. | Leave at whatever pace keeps you easy.
line @13 farewell.return : I'll hear you on the return stretch. | Good parting to the pair of us.
line @14 react.news : Give it plainly and I'll measure it for myself. | I've uncovered an ear for the whole report.
line @15 react.news.new : First hearing for these cloth-covered ears. | Our end of the street hasn't caught that word.
line @16 react.news.known : Yes. The account held its shape in transit. | I had that from an earlier telling.
line @17 react.news.doubt : A witness could settle that better than our guessing. | I'd give it time to show its true gait.
line @18 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I wish that household a gentle arrival of friends. | Terrible weight for a single threshold to bear.
line @19 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth] : Best news I've carried under this hood. | The Bright One give that household an easy season.
line @20 answer.how : Well enough to carry a bucket without slopping. | Fed, dry about the ears and glad of both.
line @21 ask.how : How's the balance between bustle and rest? | What pace has your day been setting?
line @22 decline : I'll pass; I'd have to break my word elsewhere. | I have my course set for the day already.
line @23 accept_decline : That's a clear answer. You've saved me holding my breath. | Say no once and I'll hear it properly.
line @24 sympathise : I can take the next little errand off your paws. | Stay on the dry side awhile with me.
line @25 reassure : A pause won't spoil a sound decision. | Draw breath. There's space enough for it here.
line @26 thank : That's a kindness properly placed. | I owe you a dry corner sometime.
line @27 deflect_thanks : Put the favour where it's wanted next. | It took less doing than describing.
line @28 preclose : I must turn my hood towards home. | There are little fastenings to see to yet.
line @29 accept_preclose : Go when you're ready; I'll stand clear. | You've given me plenty of your day already.
line @30 ack : Understood through the cloth. | That sounds square to me.
line @31 give.advice : Listen once before you move anything heavy. | Try the quiet way while you still have a choice.
scene toggle
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One ear of this hood stays pinned up in any weather. | #pin.capitalize# looks a poor match for that big flap.
b : Doesn't the wet get in? | Will it hold?
a : Some. I can shake off water. Can't shake a missed call back into my ear. | It has held through three pieces of cloth, which is more than I asked of it.

scene straw_listen
when topic=work self.job=herder self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's a soft scuff in the bedding just before a horse settles. | #bedding.capitalize# makes a fine loud welcome.
b : Through a door? | Loud seems an odd comfort.
a : Through a door is easier. If I stand there watching, the horse watches me back. | You can hear each step settle. No hollow knock on the stones.

scene berry_bowl
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I pick #berry# last. There's usually juice on the stalk by then. | My berry bowl has a black ring round the lip.
b : Save it for the road? | Why don't you scrub it?
a : No chance. That's the one I eat over the bowl. | Did once. A perfectly good bowl looked like it belonged to somebody else.

scene brushing
when topic=animals self.job=herder
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : What colour would you say this brush is? It was pale before the morning's work. | I've got #dust# coming out of the brush by itself.
b : The colour of whatever you last brushed. | Can it get clean?
a : Right. The beast looks splendid and I look like its shadow. | Easier out of the bristles than out of my porridge.

scene gate_check
when topic=work self.job=herder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wait for #click# before I take my paw away. | You can always tell which gate I've latched.
b : Does it sometimes need a second go? | By the sound?
a : Yes. A hasp can look shut from halfway down the yard. | By the second tug. There's a full breath between the click and the tug.

scene bucket_walk
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I walk differently carrying something that can spill. | Ever carried two full pails and felt lighter?
b : Looks almost stately. | Lighter than with one?
a : It's the water that's stately. I'm just following orders. | Much. Two sides to mind, no leaning on either.

scene uphill
when topic=dreams here.region=ridgemere
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Someday I'd like to climb the city without having to come down for something I left below. | My dream house has a view up another hill.
b : What would you carry up last? | Even if you've reached the top?
a : My hood. Everything else can go ahead without me. | A little hill will do. I like knowing I could go higher yet.

scene early_bird
when topic=animals self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I watch which of #tiles# gets a bird first. | Look how a bird shuts up shop with one foot.
b : Because that's the warm one? | Shuts up shop?
a : Because every other perch looks just as good to me. I'm hoping to learn the difference. | Tucks it away in the feathers. No latch or key to lose.

scene straw_scent
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : If I could hang a smell on a peg I'd pick clean straw. | I've a liking for #tuft# caught in a coat.
b : Why the peg? | Most would brush it off.
a : So I could come in, take one breath and hang my worries beside it. | Leave it till the next turn. Gives the street a sweeter smell.

scene clean_water
when topic=faith self.piety=devout
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I like a prayer you can carry to somebody. | Two paws to put to use while my voice thanks the Bright One.
b : Isn't a prayer spoken? | What does that mean for praying?
a : I speak it while I draw clean water. The bucket goes on to whoever needs it. | If I see a mess, both can be occupied at once.

scene wind_seam
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Wind's got up under #flap#. It wants a conversation all to itself. | A storm will find any loose stitch you've overlooked.
b : Does pinning it down help? | Is yours leaking?
a : Stops the flapping. Leaves me listening to one private little storm. | At the collar. There's a cold bead making slow progress inside.

scene cold_toggle
when topic=season|weather here.season=winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : In winter I use horn instead of metal for the hood toggle. | A cold morning makes every loose strap speak up.
b : Warmer? | What do they say?
a : Less eager to stick to a damp paw. That's warm enough. | Mostly little squeaks asking for oil.

scene hands_full
when topic=work self.job=herder self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When a horse lifts one foot for me, I keep the visit short. | I don't mind a horse nosing #bucket# while I fill it.
b : How short? | Doesn't water get everywhere?
a : Long enough to look; short enough that standing still feels worth doing again. | Yes. But I learn whether the horse wants a drink or likes pushing things.

scene sale_words
when topic=prices self.role=merchant
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : Point a fault out plainly and you have my whole attention as a seller. | There's no sense advertising legs by their length alone.
b : Some sellers would send a fault finder packing. | Doesn't length count?
a : I'd have to hear the fault from the next buyer anyway. Might as well answer now. | Certainly. But ask the buyer how long the journey is.

scene patient_animal
when topic=animals self.job=herder
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A horse doesn't mind being looked at till you start looking for a quick answer. | I stand aside when the horse wants a closer look at something.
b : Can it tell? | What if it's your coat?
a : I hurry. That's all the telling it needs. | Then it gets a nose full of oilcloth. Cures the curiosity.

scene merchant_road
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : A late wagon makes the whole street listen hard. | We've waited past the wagons' time.
b : Do they listen for wheels? | What's the worst of waiting?
a : First for wheels. Then for whoever has been sent ahead. | Giving my attention to a road that gives me nothing back.

scene new_face
when topic=newcomer|player
does offer / accept / assess
a : If you're looking for a quiet way through, I'll point one out. | I can tell you how to ask your way without drawing a little crowd.
b : Quiet sounds fine to me. | Go on, then.
a : Pick the side with the fewest open shutters. Let the noisy windows face each other. | Ask one wolf a plain question, then close your mouth till the answer comes.

scene last_stall
when topic=work|faith self.job=herder self.piety=devout
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The last stall gets the first visit when I go back through. | I like to have one creature in mind when I give thanks.
b : Why reverse your order? | Which creature?
a : Somebody always has to be last once. I see no cause to make it twice. | Whichever seemed least easy that day. It keeps my prayer from getting too grand.

scene fly_shadow
when topic=animals here.season=summer
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A fly's shadow under a hood looks large enough to pay rent. | I can hear the fly at my ear even over a whole street.
b : Is there room in there for both of you? | Surely it's quieter than the carts.
a : Until I start walking. Then I insist on travelling alone. | Much quieter. Much nearer, too.

scene berry_stain
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A purple patch on the paw is a little receipt I don't mind carrying. | I like a berry tart best once the juice starts making its escape.
b : For what purchase? | Harder to carry then.
a : An afternoon among brambles. Paid for in scratches. | Quite. Means you've got a good reason to sit down with it.

scene sleep_door
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Last night there was a little door in each fold of my hood. | In my sleep I heard somebody calling me from a closed cupboard.
b : Did you open one? | Did you recognise the voice?
a : All at once. I woke to my own hood falling off its peg. | My own. I was considerably politer from inside the cupboard.

scene misheard
when topic=accent|smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A muffled word always sounds like something you were expecting. | If I could pick a word to hear twice, it'd be the last one in a bargain.
b : How do you know? | Why the last one?
a : Because nobody mishears anything surprising till the speaker repeats it clearly. | That's the one folk drop when they think the matter's settled.

scene gossip_latch
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I like a closed mouth on a wolf who was trusted with a confidence. | A lowered voice doesn't make a piece of gossip better made.
b : Do you never want to hear the thing? | Doesn't it show care?
a : I do. But I'd rather have the reliable neighbour than the interesting afternoon. | Care about the neighbours hearing. Not about getting it right.

scene rain_pace
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's one patch on my shoulder that gets wet whenever I walk too fast. | When water runs off both sides I'm standing straight.
b : Rain keeps your pace for you? | And when it doesn't?
a : My collar does. I like the rain outside it. | Means I'm leaning in to hear. So move a little closer.

scene easy_friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I'd lend #self.friend# my last dry covering. | Good talk with #self.friend# always leaves room for a pause.
b : Even walking home afterwards? | Don't you lose the thread?
a : Especially then. A short wet walk makes no difference to a long friendship. | A sound thread waits for you to pick it up.

scene quiet_shop
when topic=work self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd put a stool outside every place of business. | I like a buyer who takes time at the door.
b : For wolves who can't pay? | Working out what to spend?
a : For any legs that have carried a wolf to my door. | Or whether to spend. I'd like the answer to be settled first.

scene first_star
when topic=faith|day here.time=dusk self.piety=devout
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My shortest thanks is for the moment I can stop watching my feet. | Supper can sit for a breath at dusk while my thanks go up.
b : What's up above, then? | Is supper inclined to listen?
a : Whatever's above the roofs. I've been looking down all day. | No. That's why the order matters.

scene hood_mend
when topic=pastimes
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : Would you hide #foldline# with a patch or leave it visible? | I'm thinking of putting my spare toggle on a cord.
b : A visible patch saves hunting next time. | Long enough to reach?
a : There's sense in having your last mistake point out the next repair. | Short enough to stay found. A long cord makes another knot to manage.

scene watch_roads
when topic=crime world.bandits=near
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : I worry less about the warnings going out than about the last cart getting one. | Bandits near the road make the quiet stretches sound different.
b : A return traveller can carry it. | You can travel alongside somebody.
a : That's the one I'd ask. A warning ought to meet a cart head on. | Yes. Two sets of ears ease the quiet considerably.

scene hard_week
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lean season makes me listen carefully to a wolf asking for a bargain. | In hard times I count the extra knot marks in a belt.
b : For what in particular? | Yours or other wolves'?
a : Whether there's something smaller that would serve just as well. | My own first. It's rude to count anybody else's till asked.

story hood_sound [topic=memories]
  : My first hood was so stiff that every time I turned my head I thought a cart had come up behind me.
  : I stepped aside for it six times along one lane. On the seventh I stood still and listened properly.
  b : Was there a cart that time?
  : Only my neck turning. I wore a fold into the cloth where my ear wanted to be.

story empty_bucket [topic=work self.job=herder]
  : I once spent a good part of a morning looking for a drip in a water pail.
  : Water went down, floor stayed dry. I sat still beside the thing till a brown nose leant past my shoulder.
  b : A horse was having a drink?
  : And waiting very civilly between my inspections.

story berry_prayer [topic=food|faith self.piety=devout]
  : I said thanks over a thornful of fruit once and put my elbow down in every berry I meant to eat.
  : I found a scrap of bread to wipe my sleeve clean; it made a rather splendid purple supper.
  ask : What would you give thanks for then?
  b : The bread and a dark-coloured sleeve.
  : Both, and enough sense to sit on the other side next time.

story feather_roof [topic=animals self.likes=roof_birds]
  : I carried a fallen feather up a stair once, hoping to learn what sort of bird had lost it.
  : Every bird on the tiles was looking the other way till the wind whipped it away over the slates.
  b : Did its owner want it back?
  : None of them. It belonged to my pillow. A bit of ticking was still caught round the end.

story straw_visitor [topic=memories self.age>=20]
  : I gave a tired stranger a seat stuffed with straw and thought I'd done well.
  : After a minute a tiny field mouse came out through the rip by the stranger's ankle.
  b : Did your visitor jump?
  : I jumped. My guest was fast asleep; the mouse had all the excitement going.

rule @hasp
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=herder
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Listen for the hasp before letting go. | Give the brown mare a clear space to turn.

rule @broom
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=herder
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That straw comes away clean underneath. | Sweep towards the opening; keep the dust behind.

rule @hurry
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dry wick, dry hood and a clear start. | Plenty of light coming. Give it a moment.

rule @berry
when concept=bark self.likes=blackberries
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That purple stain will keep till washing day. | A bramble's morning work caught in one cuff.

rule @fly
when concept=bark here.season=summer
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Here's a leaf for the loudest fly. | Off my collar, little summer nuisance.

rule @waitroad
when concept=bark world.wagons=late
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep clear where the late wheels have to turn. | Time's running faster than the wagons again.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : Something bring you round my corner? I've a little time.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, let me turn this flap back for you.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Speak near me so the neighbours can sleep through our talk.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Name your business clearly with a little space between our feet.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.job=herder] : I see to animals. The trick is hearing the trouble while it still sounds small.
dlg @6 resident.job : My work gets a clear word and a steady pull. It's mostly what anything needs.
dlg @7 resident.news [world.news] : The word that's travelled this far is #world.news#.
dlg @8 resident.news [world.wagons=raided] : There's been trouble on the wagon road. Ask the Watch before setting out.
dlg @9 resident.business [business=thriving] : A brisk trade and little time to rub the road off my boots.
dlg @10 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : They're saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I haven't witnessed it.
dlg @11 resident.bye : I'll fasten my hood again. Go dry.
dlg @12 shop.greet [here.shop=open] : Tell me what would suit you best. You'll get a fair account of the stock.
dlg @13 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : Nothing here to pass to a buyer today. You can show me what you've brought.
dlg @14 shop.prices : You're entitled to the figure before you choose. #shop_offer#
dlg @15 shop.bye : That concludes our business as I understand it. Good travelling.
graft resident.hub
choice Why pin up just one side? -> hoodpin
node hoodpin
say I want news of the street to reach an ear before it reaches the back of my head. One wet ear is a tolerable price.
choice Why not both? -> hoodrim
choice We can leave it there. -> hub
node hoodrim
say I'd have paid for an entire hood and kept only the string. I try to be sensible about my comforts.
choice I'll leave you to the street. -> bye
choice Another matter first. -> hub

graft shop.greet
choice How much time should a buyer take? -> buyerpause
node buyerpause
say Enough to ask the same question twice. If my second answer feels different from my first, I'd like to know why myself.
choice What if others are waiting? -> buyerline
choice Then I'll take a look. -> greet
node buyerline
say They can hear the answer too. Saves everyone the trouble of asking a third time.
choice Let's see what you have. -> greet
choice I'll go for now. -> bye
